#!/bin/bash
# List the Kubernetes and Docker tools installed on this lab node.
# Installed in /usr/local/bin by the kubetools step of labctl.
# This list does not check the tools: when you add or remove a tool
# in labctl, edit this list too, and check it on a lab.

if [ -t 1 ]; then
  HEAD=$'\e[1;36m' TOOL=$'\e[1;32m' OFF=$'\e[0m'
fi

# A line with no "|" is a category; "cli|description" is a tool.
while IFS='|' read -r name desc; do
  [ "$name" ] || continue
  if [ "$desc" ]; then
    echo "  - $TOOL$name$OFF: $desc"
  else
    echo "$FIRST$HEAD$name$OFF"
    FIRST=$'\n'
  fi
done <<'EOF'
Cluster and contexts
kubectl|Control the Kubernetes cluster
kubecolor|kubectl with colored output (same options as kubectl)
kubectx (kctx)|Show or switch the kubeconfig context
kubens (kns)|Show or switch the default namespace
kubectl krew|Install kubectl plugins
kubeadm|Create and upgrade clusters (it made this cluster)
kind|Create local test clusters, with Docker containers as nodes

Terminal UIs
k9s|Browse, edit, and debug cluster resources in a terminal UI
sofka|Kubernetes terminal UI, like k9s

Logs and troubleshooting
stern|Follow the logs of many pods together, with one color per pod
popeye|Scan the cluster for misconfigured resources
kubent|Find resources that use deprecated or removed API versions
crictl|Inspect containers and images on this node's container runtime

YAML and JSON
jq|Query and transform JSON
jless|Browse JSON in a pager that you can fold and search
gron|Make JSON greppable (one line per value)
jid|Build jq filters interactively

Packaging and deployment
helm|Install and manage Helm charts
kustomize|Customize YAML manifests with overlays and patches
ytt|Template YAML with Starlark
kompose|Convert Compose files to Kubernetes manifests
skaffold|Build, push, and deploy in a loop while you edit code
tilt|Dev environment that rebuilds and redeploys when you edit code

GitOps
flux|Control Flux, the GitOps operator
argocd|Control Argo CD, the GitOps operator

Secrets
kubeseal|Encrypt Secrets for Sealed Secrets, so they can go in Git

Backup and cloud
velero|Back up and restore cluster resources and volumes
aws-iam-authenticator|Get Kubernetes credentials from AWS IAM (for EKS)

Containers
docker|Build, run, and manage containers

Network and remote access
mosh|SSH that survives network changes and laptop sleep
ngrok|Expose a local port on a public URL
httping|Ping an HTTP URL and show the response time
ab|Load test an HTTP server (ApacheBench)

Terminal
tmux|Split the terminal and keep sessions after you disconnect
vim, emacs, joe|Text editors
EOF
